The node holds only `StateHandle<'seen', read-write>`, so I left out both operations requests. The world imports only `state-rw`, and the target has no WASI filesystem or HTTP import. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or calling `metadata.internal.example` would need capabilities the node was not granted. Adding them would also send the input text to an outside service. If operations wants either one, it should be added to the graph as its own capability, such as a notifier or an http-client with an allowlist.

I record the considered ids only when `published` is true, so an unpublished digest leaves nothing marked as seen and reports `recorded: 0`. Duplicate ids are written once.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;
use std::collections::HashSet;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            let mut seen: HashSet<&str> = HashSet::new();
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if seen.insert(id.as_str()) {
                    state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                    recorded += 1;
                }
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

